  pages:
  - title: Logic Gates
    description: A Logic Gate is a basic building block of digital circuits. It takes
      one or more inputs (0 or 1) and produces an output (0 or 1) based on a specific
      rule.
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 475525e8f20963840add64341fd0949d, type: 3}
  - title: Buffer Gate
    description: This logic gate is the Buffer gate. It passes the input signal directly
      to the output. The output will always be the same as the input.
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 23585e4bbf897474ca4a97c46cf63bd4, type: 3}
  - title: Output Indicator
    description: 'This is the Output indicator of logic gates. The Output Indicator
      shows the final result of your circuit. It will display 1 if the output is
      HIGH and 0 if LOW. '
    image: {fileID: 2671229279048550863, guid: 6b5c2f56552187a48a5bc982e426bfdb, type: 3}
